From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:03:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nwm::CEC: answer the StreetPass radio quietly (Build 132)

Once a game has StreetPass on (Nintendogs + Cats with 0131), the real
StreetPass module keeps looking for 3DS consoles nearby through nwm::CEC,
which Tangelo doesn't implement: about 1,060 "unknown / unimplemented
function" lines in a short session (0x0002 846 times, 0x001D/0x000A/0x0006/
0x001C about 50 each, SendProbeRequest and a few others).

An emulator has no 3DS radio (StreetPass goes over the internet with
NetPass), so every nwm::CEC command now gets the same reply as before
(success, no data = nobody nearby) from a handler that logs each command
once at info level and the rest at debug level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
